Update wllama's common_fit_params stub to llama.cpp's new signature.

wllama replaces llama.cpp's device-memory fitting with a stub in
cpp/wllama-context.h that always returns COMMON_PARAMS_FIT_STATUS_FAILURE
(there is no device fitting to do in a browser). llama.cpp d7d1b632d
changed the first parameter from a single model path (const char *) to a
list of model paths (const std::vector<std::string> &), so the stub no
longer matches the calls in common.cpp and the link failed. The stub
ignores its arguments, so only the signature changes; behaviour is
identical to the old pin. common/fit.cpp therefore stays excluded
(patch 0011).

diff --git a/cpp/wllama-context.h b/cpp/wllama-context.h
index 3e9e1c0..e1850be 100644
--- a/cpp/wllama-context.h
+++ b/cpp/wllama-context.h
@@ -1329,7 +1329,7 @@ void common_log_default_callback(enum ggml_log_level level, const char *text, vo
 }
 
 enum common_params_fit_status common_fit_params(
-    const char *path_model,
+    const std::vector<std::string> &paths_model,
     llama_model_params *mparams,
     llama_context_params *cparams,
     float *tensor_split,
